│                          │ specialized for the Heilbronn problem. The construction anchors the three extreme         │
│                          │ vertices of the containing equilateral triangle, then searches over barycentric           │
│                          │ coordinates for the remaining eight points. This parameterization guarantees feasibility  │
│                          │ at every optimization step.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The primary search uses seeded differential evolution to escape poor local arrangements.  │
│                          │ Its best candidate is then polished using the epigraph formulation of the max-min-area    │
│                          │ problem: an auxiliary variable t is maximized subject to every one of the 165 triangle    │
│                          │ areas being at least t. This is substantially better aligned with the actual evaluation   │
│                          │ criterion than optimizing a surrogate such as average area. A deterministic               │
│                          │ random/local-search fallback keeps the function usable when SciPy is unavailable or an    │
│                          │ optimizer fails.                                                                          │
