│ patch_description        │ The previous annealer selects movable points uniformly. In a maximin triangle-area        │
│                          │ problem, most points are irrelevant to the current objective at any given step: the       │
│                          │ objective is controlled by a small set of nearly minimum-area triples. Selecting a point  │
│                          │ from one of these active constraints directs mutations toward the geometry actually       │
│                          │ limiting the score, while retaining occasional uniform moves for global exploration.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The final stage is also changed from fixed-scale random greedy perturbations into a       │
│                          │ deterministic active-constraint polishing schedule. Its decreasing radius permits         │
│                          │ meaningful corrections first and fine adjustment later, and it explicitly identifies      │
│                          │ near-worst triples before choosing a participating non-vertex point. This should          │
│                          │ substantially improve the final minimum area without increasing the number of expensive   │
│                          │ objective evaluations.                                                                    │
