│ patch_name               │ active_set_polish                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic active-set-style coordinate polishing phase after annealing. The      │
│                          │ annealer is effective at finding the broad combinatorial structure, but its final         │
│                          │ proposals still accept thermal regressions and therefore often leave avoidable slack in   │
│                          │ the smallest determinant constraints. The added phase performs strictly improving maximin │
│                          │ moves in barycentric coordinates, trying several local perturbations for each non-vertex  │
│                          │ point at progressively smaller radii. Comparisons are lexicographic: normalized minimum   │
│                          │ area is never sacrificed, while the existing tail merit breaks ties and helps avoid       │
│                          │ immediately recreating another nearly-degenerate triangle.                                │
