│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ softmin_annealing                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace purely minimum-area Metropolis decisions with a lower-tail soft-min energy. The   │
│                          │ raw minimum is highly nonsmooth: moving a point often improves one active triangle only   │
│                          │ to expose another nearly active triangle, so a move can be rejected despite improving the │
│                          │ local bottleneck structure. A soft-min energy simultaneously penalizes all small-area     │
│                          │ triples, providing a substantially smoother continuation objective early in the search,   │
│                          │ while cooling it toward the true minimum-area objective near the end. The returned        │
│                          │ incumbent is still selected exclusively by the exact minimum normalized area.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The same change also makes proposal selection consider all triangles in the lower tail    │
│                          │ rather than only the single worst triple, avoiding repeated attempts to move a point when │
│                          │ a cluster of nearly tied constraints is responsible.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0230                                                                                   │
