│ patch_name               │ oriented_epigraph_search                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces nonsmooth absolute-area polishing with an oriented-matroid epigraph │
│                          │ formulation. Differential evolution first identifies a promising combinatorial            │
│                          │ orientation cell. Within that cell, every triangle orientation has a fixed sign, so the   │
│                          │ absolute determinant constraints become smooth signed quadratic inequalities. SLSQP then  │
│                          │ maximizes an explicit minimum-area variable using analytic Jacobians for all 165 triangle │
│                          │ constraints, substantially improving local convergence and avoiding the kinked            │
│                          │ absolute-value constraints used previously.                                               │
