│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_constraint_directional_polish                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the final “single worst triangle” axis-aligned polish with an active-constraint   │
│                          │ directional search. In a maximin Heilbronn configuration, several nearly minimal          │
│                          │ determinants are normally simultaneously tight, so improving only the arbitrarily         │
│                          │ selected minimum triple often traps the search by worsening another almost-active triple. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new refinement collects all triples within a small tolerance of the current lower     │
│                          │ tail, visits every movable point participating in them, and tests a deterministic         │
│                          │ stencil. Besides simplex-coordinate directions, the stencil includes directions toward    │
│                          │ and away from the centroid of each active triangle’s other two vertices. These            │
│                          │ partner-centroid directions directly alter the restrictive determinant and are            │
│                          │ substantially better aligned with the nonsmooth maximin geometry than axis steps.         │
│                          │ Candidate acceptance is lexicographic: first improve the exact minimum, then improve the  │
│                          │ mean of the lower tail when the minimum is tied. This preserves the primary objective     │
│                          │ while resolving degeneracies and preparing further minimum increases.                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
