│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ elite_de_polish                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 9 independent single-point simulated-annealing restarts with    │
│                          │ 18,000 iterations each, random Dirichlet initialization, a fixed cooling schedule, and    │
│                          │ only retains one global best configuration. Its main limitations are that the initial     │
│                          │ configurations are not strongly competitive, promising local basins are discarded, and    │
│                          │ late-stage refinement only follows one search trajectory.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version uses a two-stage deterministic search:                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. A vectorized differential-evolution population phase (`population_size=72`,            │
│                          │ `generations=720`) builds substantially better global arrangements than independent       │
│                          │ random annealing.                                                                         │
│                          │ 2. The best `elite_count=6` population endpoints are retained using a combined            │
│                          │ minimum-area / low-tail merit score.                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Each elite endpoint receives a targeted active-constraint annealing polish             │
│                          │ (`polish_iterations=10500`). Points occurring in the currently smallest triangles are     │
│                          │ perturbed more often, while occasional unrestricted moves preserve escape capability.     │
│                          │ 4. The cooling schedule and proposal radius are adaptive, with relatively large early     │
│                          │ barycentric perturbations and much finer late refinement.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The objective remains the true normalized minimum triangle determinant, while the         │
│                          │ low-tail merit improves movement across tied or near-active constraints.                  │
