│ patch_name               │ structured_polish11                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This version uses a deterministic hybrid search designed specifically for the             │
│                          │ eleven-point Heilbronn triangle problem. It keeps the three outer vertices fixed,         │
│                          │ explores both structured boundary/interior templates and Dirichlet-distributed starts,    │
│                          │ then performs adaptive simulated-annealing mutations focused on points participating in   │
│                          │ small-area triangles.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strongest candidates from all restarts are subsequently polished with SLSQP using the │
│                          │ fixed orientation pattern of all triangle determinants. This converts the final local     │
│                          │ stage into a constrained maximin optimization problem. The implementation caches its      │
│                          │ final result, uses vectorized determinant evaluation, includes feasibility validation,    │
│                          │ and retains a safe valid fallback if SciPy optimization is unavailable or fails.          │
