│ patch_name               │ template_diverse_restarts                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace purely interior-biased Dirichlet restart initialization with a deterministic      │
│                          │ mixture of geometric templates and boundary-seeking Dirichlet samples. In the             │
│                          │ eleven-point Heilbronn problem, strong configurations commonly contain points close to    │
│                          │ each of the three sides together with a staggered interior core; ordinary Dirichlet       │
│                          │ samples often fail to enter these order types. The templates place one point near each    │
│                          │ side and five non-collinear interior points, then apply reproducible small barycentric    │
│                          │ jitter. The remaining restarts retain random exploration, including lower-concentration   │
│                          │ Dirichlet draws that more frequently sample edge-near configurations. This changes only   │
│                          │ initialization, preserving the established annealing and SLSQP polish machinery.          │
