│ patch_name               │ active_set_linesearch_polish                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the final single-worst-triangle coordinate polish with a deterministic active-set │
│                          │ refinement. Heilbronn optima are governed by several nearly tied triangle constraints, so │
│                          │ moving only points of one arbitrarily selected minimum triangle often stalls immediately. │
│                          │ The new polish considers all near-active triples, generates axial, simplex-diagonal,      │
│                          │ partner-centroid, and boundary-tangent directions, and performs a short deterministic     │
│                          │ line search at several displacement lengths. This is particularly useful near simplex     │
│                          │ boundaries, where projection changes the effective direction of a move. Candidates are    │
│                          │ still accepted only on a strict improvement of the true minimum area, preserving the      │
│                          │ primary objective exactly.                                                                │
