│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_coupled_annealing                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace uniformly selected single-point mutations with bottleneck-driven proposals. In    │
│                          │ maximin Heilbronn search, the limiting constraints are a small set of low-area triples,   │
│                          │ so selecting points that participate in these triples concentrates work where it can      │
│                          │ increase the true objective. With moderate probability, the edit also selects a second    │
│                          │ active free point from the same low-area structure and moves both points jointly. This is │
│                          │ important because many locally competitive order types require coordinated displacement   │
│                          │ of two points to relax several active determinant constraints simultaneously; independent │
│                          │ moves often worsen another active triple and are rejected. The proposal retains           │
│                          │ occasional uniform selection and broad early relocation to preserve order-type            │
│                          │ exploration and remains fully deterministic under the existing generator seed.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0311                                                                                   │
