│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ phased_tail_anneal                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current search uses 8 restarts of 30,000 iterations, a single log-sum-exp tail scale  │
│                          │ schedule, 90% active-triple point selection, and one-point random perturbations. Its main │
│                          │ limitation is that early log-sum-exp pressure can concentrate on a small set of currently │
│                          │ active determinants before a globally favorable combinatorial structure is discovered.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This revision uses 11 shorter but more diverse restarts, including boundary-biased        │
│                          │ simplex initializations, and a phase-dependent lower-tail objective. Early search rewards │
│                          │ the mean of the lowest 30 determinants and a broad soft-min surrogate, encouraging global │
│                          │ separation. The tail width is progressively narrowed to 10 determinants while the exact   │
│                          │ minimum receives increasing weight during the final phase. Proposals use                  │
│                          │ barycentric-weight perturbations rather than Cartesian clipping, preserving simplex       │
│                          │ feasibility more smoothly. A small proportion of coordinated two-point moves helps escape │
│                          │ poor oriented-matroid cells. Final polishing uses active-set directions plus random       │
│                          │ tangential simplex directions and prioritizes exact maximin improvement.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0585                                                                                   │
