│ patch_name               │ active_coupled_annealing                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Restore bottleneck-directed search during annealing. Uniform single-point mutations spend │
│                          │ most evaluations moving points that do not participate in the limiting triangles. This    │
│                          │ edit identifies points appearing in the lowest-area triples and preferentially moves      │
│                          │ them. It also adds occasional coordinated two-point proposals: tightly constrained        │
│                          │ arrangements often require two points to move together to relax intersecting active       │
│                          │ determinant constraints, which cannot be achieved by a one-point mutation without         │
│                          │ worsening another active triple. The proposal remains deterministic under the existing    │
│                          │ fixed generator and retains uniform mutations for order-type exploration.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
