│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ phased_de_epigraph                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The prior program uses a single SciPy differential-evolution run (`popsize=23`,           │
│                          │ `maxiter=520`) on the exact nonsmooth minimum, then attempts signed epigraph polishing    │
│                          │ from only one orientation cell. This can converge to a mediocre combinatorial cell and    │
│                          │ has relatively high evaluation cost.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version uses a deterministic vectorized differential-evolution population (`96`      │
│                          │ candidates, `760` generations) directly in simplex coordinates. Its selection score is    │
│                          │ phase-dependent: early generations use the mean of the lowest `30` determinants with low  │
│                          │ weight to discover globally separated layouts; later generations narrow to the lowest     │
│                          │ `10` constraints and increase tail weight, encouraging active-constraint equalization     │
│                          │ before exact epigraph polishing. Several final elites are independently polished by SLSQP │
│                          │ rather than trusting one global-search winner. Mutation changes from exploratory          │
│                          │ DE/rand/1 to best-directed updates, and feasibility is maintained by barycentric simplex  │
│                          │ projection.                                                                               │
