│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_set_linesearch                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic, boundary-aware active-set line search immediately before the signed  │
│                          │ epigraph solve. Differential evolution often identifies the correct orientation cell but  │
│                          │ leaves several nearly active triangle constraints slightly unbalanced. A short greedy     │
│                          │ refinement over axial, diagonal, partner-centroid, and simplex-edge tangent directions    │
│                          │ can improve that balance without the cost or noise of another global search.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The refinement only accepts moves preserving the true minimum area up to numerical        │
│                          │ tolerance, using the low-area tail as a secondary criterion. It therefore cannot degrade  │
│                          │ the returned configuration, while providing SLSQP with a better-conditioned point in the  │
│                          │ same oriented-matroid cell. Edge tangents are explicitly included when points are near a  │
│                          │ simplex boundary, where ordinary projected displacements can be strongly distorted.       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0557                                                                                   │
